---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DataTable from '../../components/DataTable.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="UniDPP is an open, multi-body initiative: CalConnect, ISO/TC 154, OIML, ELF, Enosema, and the UnitsML coalition each steward a layer. Apache-2.0 / MIT licensing."
  eyebrow="04 · Reference — about"
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    UniDPP is an open, multi-body initiative. No single organization owns the framework:
    each steward body is responsible for the layer it already operates as an international
    standards activity, and the software is developed in the open under permissive
    licences.
  </p>

  <section id="stewardship" class="plate" aria-labelledby="stewardship-h">
    <h2 id="stewardship-h">Stewardship</h2>
    <DataTable
      columns={['Body', 'Responsibility']}
      rows={[
        ['<strong>CalConnect</strong>', 'Project home; terminology; time, events, and the state machine; offline freshness; SIGNATIF with TC 154; the UnitsML quantity chain.'],
        ['<strong>ISO/TC 154</strong>', 'Identity; trade-documented seams; registry governance with UN/CEFACT; issuance rules; the NWIP vehicle.'],
        ['<strong>OIML</strong>', 'Measurement validity and decision rules; CNML/ESDC; issuance-role governance; the first vertical pilot; the twin ladder.'],
        ['<strong>ELF</strong>', 'The EXPRESS core; seam contracts (S3/S8); the mapping technical report; the AP242 identity-lattice lineage; OpenCDD dictionary technology.'],
        ['<strong>Enosema</strong>', 'FERIN registry operations; ISO 19135:2025 expressibility guarantees.'],
        ['<strong>UnitsML coalition</strong>', 'The quantity chain: ISO 80000 → UnitsDB/UnitsML → OpenCDD.'],
      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <section id="governance" aria-labelledby="governance-h">
    <h2 id="governance-h">Governance and licensing</h2>
    <p>
      The standards work is carried in ISO/IEC JTC 5 and partner bodies — ISO/TC 154,
      OIML, UN/CEFACT, and CEN where the European profile requires it — and is contributed
      through national member bodies and liaison channels. The project contributes
      implementation experience and datasets; it does not create a rival standards track.
    </p>
    <p>
      The software is licensed Apache-2.0 or MIT per repository; the website and the
      terminology dataset are MIT. There is no closed core and no boundary package around
      a private backend: every algorithm the framework specifies is published with a
      conformance suite.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guardrails the project holds to: the EN series’ own neutrality language is enforced
      rather than amended; no rival central registry — the multi-log quorum answers “who
      runs it”; the terminology absorbs no AAS vocabulary outside an informative annex;
      and internal discipline first — one canonical units chain, one registry, one trust
      framework.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
    <h2 id="contact-h">Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Source: <a href="https://github.com/unidpp">github.com/unidpp</a></li>
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@unidpp.org">contact@unidpp.org</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
